wifi: mt76: mt7925: clear DROP_PROBEREQ in RX filter for AP mode

mt7925_configure_filter() only manipulates a 3-bit FIF mask
(FCSFAIL, CONTROL, OTHER_BSS) and never clears
MT_WF_RFCR_DROP_PROBEREQ from the connac3 RX filter. As a result,
the firmware drops directed probe requests before they reach
mac80211, and the AP never generates probe responses.

STAs that need probe response refresh to keep a BSS in their scan
cache (notably Qualcomm-based clients such as the Xiaomi 14 Ultra)
cycle indefinitely between scan and "no_bss_found" and cannot
establish a connection. STAs that do not strictly require probe
responses (e.g. HiSilicon-based) can still associate, which masks
the bug on some hardware combinations.

Bringing up a monitor interface as a workaround happens to fix
the issue because the monitor mode setup goes through a different
MCU command path that bypasses the per-VIF filter.

Every other mt76 driver clears this bit explicitly: mt7603/main.c,
mt7615/main.c, mt7915/main.c, mt7996/main.c. Bring mt7925 in line
by adding a second mt7925_mcu_set_rxfilter() call that clears
MT_WF_RFCR_DROP_PROBEREQ via the bitmap interface that
mt7925_mcu_set_beacon_filter() already uses for
MT_WF_RFCR_DROP_OTHER_BEACON.

Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <floss@jetm.me>
Reported-by: SerialVelocity <SerialVelocity@users.noreply.github.com>
Closes: https://github.com/jetm/mediatek-mt7927-dkms/issues/61
Fixes: c948b5da6bbe ("wifi: mt76: mt7925: add Mediatek Wi-Fi7 driver for mt7925 chips")

e5d1e64b7361547c5cbde5feee96dfdee94e9ac2
diff --git a/mt7925/main.c b/mt7925/main.c
index 844f8ff..bfaebeb 100644
--- a/mt7925/main.c
+++ b/mt7925/main.c
@@ -840,2 +840,3 @@ static void mt7925_configure_filter(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 #define MT7925_FILTER_ENABLE     BIT(31)
+#define MT7925_FIF_BIT_CLR       BIT(1)
 	struct mt792x_dev *dev = mt792x_hw_dev(hw);
@@ -854,2 +855,4 @@ static void mt7925_configure_filter(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 	mt7925_mcu_set_rxfilter(dev, flags, 0, 0);
+	mt7925_mcu_set_rxfilter(dev, 0, MT7925_FIF_BIT_CLR,
+				MT_WF_RFCR_DROP_PROBEREQ);
 	mt792x_mutex_release(dev);
